2026-11-09 21:07 cpanfile audit and minimum versions (branch k22-k25, uncommitted yet). Only cpanfile changed.

Removed: Pod::Weaver::Section::Support 1.014 - last used as _exp('Support'), replaced by GenerateSection in 1396f5c (2026-01-11); today @GETTY/Support is Author::GETTY::Support (a GenerateSection subclass); nothing in lib/ loads or hooks it in. Consumers under [@Author::GETTY] never read their own weaver.ini (the bundle always sets config_plugin, DZP::PodWeaver 4.010), so nothing relies on the transitive install.
Added runtime: perl 5.022; Moose (use Moose in 9 files); namespace::autoclean (Transformer, Legal, Support). Added on test: Module::Runtime (t/no_cpan_release.t), Software::License (t/binary-config.t and others). recommends PAR::Packer now 1.031.

Rule: one line per CPAN distribution whose code lib/ loads or hooks in by name (plugin, bundle, weaver section/plugin, transformer, fallback_version_provider, a command in a default config string such as cpanm). The line names the addressed or main module; its version pins a release and so covers every module of that release (Git::*, Dist::Zilla core plugins, Pod::Weaver sections, Pod::Elemental elements, Run::* get no line of their own). An extra line only when a module of another, brought-along distribution needs more than that distribution guarantees (checked for RewriteVersion::Transitional and BumpVersionAfterRelease via @Git::VersionManager: not needed). Runtime lines are not repeated under on test. Core (Module::CoreList for 5.022) is not listed unless a newer version is needed. Deliberate step from the older silent rule "comes with Dist::Zilla": Moose and namespace::autoclean are now listed, following 88a07c4, which declared Path::Tiny, Config::Identity and Pithub despite their transitive origin.

Workflow scripts (.github/dzil-binary/*.pl): not runtime prereqs of the bundle. They run in dzil-binary.yml under the leg's own packing perl from the checkout, never from an installed [@Author::GETTY]; build-leg.sh installs PAR::Packer there, which brings Archive::Zip. Because t/binary-scripts.t requires them, their only non-core need, Archive::Zip, stays under on test; everything else they load (JSON::PP, Digest::SHA, File::Find, File::Temp, File::Path, POSIX, Time::HiRes, Cwd, File::Basename, File::Spec) is core from 5.22.

